<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bretton Woods system</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1944–1971</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bretton Woods system was the international monetary order agreed at the Bretton Woods Conference in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-hampshire">New Hampshire</a> in July 1944. It fixed exchange rates against the US dollar, which was convertible into gold at 35 dollars an ounce, and created the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/international-monetary-fund">International Monetary Fund</a> and the World Bank; it broke down after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> ended gold convertibility in 1971.</p></div>
